<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mindelheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mindelheim is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindel">Mindel</a> river. It belonged to the Frundsberg family, whose best-known member, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> commander Georg von Frundsberg, was born there, and later to Bavaria. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-blenheim">Battle of Blenheim</a> the emperor granted it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-churchill-1st-duke-of-marlborough">Duke of Marlborough</a> as a principality in 1705, but it was returned to Bavaria in 1714.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mindelheim.jpg" alt="Mindelheim" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marienplatz,_Mindelheim,_Alemania,_2019-06-21,_DD_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
